From: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] cmm_wpa: Generate RSNEs for FT-only security modes

WPAMakeRSNIE() omits FT-EAP, FT-SAE and FT-EAP-SHA384 when deciding
whether to generate an RSNE. Configurations containing only these suites
therefore leave the RSNE length at zero, although WPAMakeRsnIeAKM()
already supports their encoding.

Include these suites in the RSNE generation condition under
DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT.

Signed-off-by: chasey-dev <ellenyoung0912@gmail.com>
---
--- a/mt_wifi/common/security/cmm_wpa.c
+++ b/mt_wifi/common/security/cmm_wpa.c
@@ -2398,7 +2398,11 @@ VOID WPAMakeRSNIE (
 	    IS_AKM_WPA2PSK(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
 	    IS_AKM_WPA3PSK(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
 #ifdef DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT
+	    /* Hostapd can advertise FT suites without their non-FT variants. */
+	    IS_AKM_FT_WPA2(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
 	    IS_AKM_FT_WPA2PSK(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
+	    IS_AKM_FT_SAE_SHA256(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
+	    IS_AKM_FT_WPA2_SHA384(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
 	    IS_AKM_FT_SAE_EXT(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
 #endif /* DOT11R_FT_SUPPORT */
 	    IS_AKM_DPP(pSecConfig->AKMMap) ||
